#
# RESEED (hand-harvest, local on fix/retirement, forward-only): the §16 SYSCALL POINTER-BRIDGE intrinsics
# (`ptr_word`/`ref_word`) + the `SYS_WRITE` proof — the second syscall crumb, letting a buffer/struct address
# cross into a syscall register slot without libc. What this harvest carries:
#   - **§16 syscall bridges (compiler — checker + codegen)**:
#     - `teko::sys::ptr_word(p: ptr): i64` — ordinary builtin (`scope.tks`, beside the `syscallN` family),
#       lowering (`emit_ptr_word`, hooked in the `as_cstr`/`buf_ptr` special-arm chain) to
#       `((int64_t)(uintptr_t)(<p>))`. Takes an opaque `ptr` (e.g. from `teko::mem::as_cstr`) — the widening
#       rides the existing `ptr_widens_to_opaque` path (the `bytes_from_ptr` precedent) — and yields its address
#       as an `i64` for a syscall arg. The sanctioned opaque→int reinterpret, on the `f64_bits` carve-out.
#     - `teko::sys::ref_word(x): i64` — an lvalue-checked SPECIAL form (`type_ref_word` in `typer.tks`, mirroring
#       `type_ptr_unwrap`'s addressable-`var` proof, no type argument), lowering (`emit_ref_word`) to
#       `((int64_t)(uintptr_t)&(<x>))`. A `lookup_call` check lets a real user `ref_word` declaration win over the
#       intrinsic (declaration-beats-fallback). Unused by this crumb; wired for the next (`clock_gettime`).
#     - `teko::sys::SYS_WRITE` (`sys.tks`): x86_64(1)/aarch64(64), `#os("linux") #arch(...)`-guarded.
#
# NOT INERT IN SOURCE, BUT NO BEHAVIORAL CORPUS DIVERGENCE. The compiler's own corpus (`src/`) calls neither
# bridge nor any syscall, so both intrinsics — pure expression-level lowerings, no preamble helper — are fully
# inert on the self-image; the emitted C differs from the previous seed only by the new checker/codegen SOURCE
# plus the mechanical line/offset shifts it induces (a function-add reseed). Verified: the `(int64_t)(uintptr_t)`
# casts + `tk_syscall3` helper appear as real emitted C only in the sys_write fixture's output, and in the
# compiler's own teko.c only as quoted string literals inside `emit_ptr_word`/`emit_ref_word`/the syscall
# emitter's own source — genuinely use-gated.
#
# NATIVE LEG — HONEST-STOP (by design). The bridges lower only on the C leg; native lowering is DEFERRED to the
# terminal native-correction phase of Doc-2. The C leg is the target.
